AltoReferralWhitelistAdapter::getBonusRewardInfo
├── when user has no referral address set
│   └── it should return zero bonus info
├── when user has referral address set to zero
│   └── it should return zero bonus info
├── when referral address is not whitelisted
│   └── it should return zero bonus info
└── when referral address is valid and whitelisted
    ├── when user has valid referral setup
    │   ├── it should return configured bonus discount
    │   ├── it should return configured payment token share
    │   └── it should return referral address as payment token share receiver
    ├── when multiple users have same referral address
    │   ├── it should return same bonus info for all users
    │   └── it should return same referral address as receiver
    ├── when adapter configuration changes after referral set
    │   ├── it should return updated bonus discount
    │   ├── it should return updated payment token share
    │   └── it should return same referral address as receiver
    ├── when referral address is removed from whitelist after setting
    │   └── it should return zero bonus info
    └── when calling for different users with different setups
        ├── it should return appropriate bonus info for each user
        └── it should maintain independent states
